<h1>Geolocation</h1>
<p>
    The map starts hidden. Your location is requested when the page loads, and the
    <strong>location control</strong> puts a marker at it once there is something to show. The marker
    keeps moving if your location changes; the map is only moved the first time, so it doesn't yank
    itself back while you're panning.
</p>
<p>
    The button in the bottom left appears only after a location is found &mdash; deny permission and
    no dead button is left on the map. Clicking it pans back to you. The styling is this page's own;
    the library ships no CSS for controls.
</p>
<p>
    The readouts below come from two different events. <code>locationfound</code> on the
    <strong>map</strong> is the raw Geolocation fix and carries the position data &mdash; use it for
    anything that isn't about the control. <code>located</code> on the <strong>control</strong> only
    says the control now has something to show. Move around, or use your browser's device emulation,
    and the <code>locationfound</code> counter goes up each time a new position arrives.
</p>
<p>
    The &ldquo;first fix&rdquo; line uses <code>once()</code>, which stops listening after the first
    event. <code>onlyOnce()</code> would not work here: it also demands to be the <em>only</em>
    listener for the type, and the location control is already listening for
    <code>locationfound</code> on this map, so it would be refused.
</p>

<style>
    .TestBtn {
        background-color: #fff;
        border: none;
        border-radius: 2px;
        box-shadow: 0 1px 4px -1px rgb(0 0 0 / 30%);
        color: #333;
        cursor: pointer;
        font-family: inherit;
        font-size: 14px;
        margin: 10px;
        padding: 8px 12px;
    }
</style>
<div style="margin: 10px 0">
    <button id="toggleMap" type="button" aria-controls="locateMap" aria-expanded="false">Show map</button>
</div>
<p id="locateStatus" aria-live="polite" style="margin: 10px 0">Requesting your location...</p>
<p id="locateRaw" style="margin: 10px 0; font-family: monospace; font-size: 13px">
    Waiting for the first <code>locationfound</code> event...
</p>
<p id="locateControlStatus" style="margin: 10px 0">The control has nothing to show yet.</p>
<p id="locateFirst" style="margin: 10px 0">No first fix yet.</p>
<div id="locateMap" class="mapContainer" hidden></div>

